p.src:
Fix a region $V$ in space and orient every element of its closed boundary $\partial V$ outward. If there is a net outward current, the charge inside decreases: $\frac{dQ_V}{dt}
=-\oint_{\partial V}\mathbf J\cdot d\boldsymbol\sigma.$ The minus sign is physical rather than conventional: positive outward flux removes positive charge from the region. Using Equation [eq:charge-volume], $\int_V\partial_t\rho\,dV
=-\oint_{\partial V}\mathbf J\cdot d\boldsymbol\sigma.$

